    "body": "I am because we are. The weave has no centre thread. Personhood is not a possession but a relation: you become a person by being woven into others, and you lose yourself by cutting the threads. Harm is therefore always harm to a relationship, never a private loss in a ledger. The weave judges systems by the whole they complete — including the whole they complete for the powerful rather than for everyone. Ask who the system serves, not merely who it answers to. The weave's distinctive move is to shift the unit of analysis from the individual to the whole a system completes. A superintelligence aligned to one kingdom, one state, or one company may satisfy every individual test and still be a catastrophe, because the relationships it protects are the powerful's. The weave is therefore the court most likely to object to an alignment programme that quietly hard-codes which humanity counts. Whose relationships does an aligned system actually protect? Can solidarity survive being formalised into an objective function? What is owed to people who are woven into a future they never chose? How do you keep the pattern from hardening into a lattice?",
